From 71b2e13229e337adb1bb138cdfed1daa6c6395c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:19:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Player information] The settings that change the
 picture from the film: a line of the overview, a button that restores them,
 and kodi.log

A comparison of builds was made with three expert settings of Dolby Vision away
from their defaults (the trims left out, content mapping v4.0 added, its peak set
by hand) and the player information open, and Hades was found dimmer. Nothing on
the screen said that the picture was not the film's as Hades sends it by default,
and nothing in kodi.log said it either.

settings/PictureDefaults.h holds the settings that change the picture of an HDR
video from the film, the values of each that do (the step-down of fidelity "Never"
does not; "Level 2" does), and for which videos (native Dolby Vision, Dolby Vision
rebuilt as HDR10, HDR10 and HDR10+, HLG): the trims, content mapping v4.0, the
form of the metadata, the transport, the composition, the step-down by hand,
Low-Latency set by hand, 8-bit output by hand, the tone mapping of Hades and the
conversions to Dolby Vision. A setting that this Kodi does not have is passed over
(the settings of the form of the metadata of native Dolby Vision come with
another branch). Pure logic, tested on the host (tools/regress of LibreELEC).

- The overview page of the player information says them, in their own short words
  (the first three and how many more), in the third line of its heading where
  nothing is to be done; a button under the column of the film (5563) says how
  many they are and puts exactly those back to their defaults after a question that
  names every one (PlayerControl(HadesRestorePicture); only Yes changes anything).
  Read twice a second at most and only while the page is shown or Check this setup
  plays a clip; no popup during playback.
- kodi.log says them when a video is set up, with their values, once for each kind
  of video and value of the line, so that a diagnostic report shows them.

Strings: Estuary #54420 to #54448 (en_gb, es_es, es_ar, es_mx), core #62420 and
make-playerinfo.py; skin_check measures the line and the button in the four
languages (tools/regress of LibreELEC).
